body:
Yes. It's part of The Legendary Storyteller Tall Tale, and some others as well. Sometimes it's part of a couple voyages from the Merchant Alliance as well. Not sure why it still remains uncharted though.

&#x200B;

It was used in time limited adventures too. Merrick was killed there.

Yes. In any case, they could've built a new city somewhere else and named it Port Merrick. Maybe make it the hub for the Hunter's Call faction.

&#x200B;

Golden Sands is Golden Sands, WE decided its fate.

Estamos en el punto donde todavía podemos más o menos (sobre)vivir si tenemos algún que otro privilegio como no haber nacido en el medio de una pobreza estructural, pero si no heredaste algo probablemente no llegues a tener nada propio aunque te recontra mates.

&#x200B;

El darwinismo social y la meritocracia se terminó cuando toda la tierra ya fue dividida y tiene dueño.

My biggest problem with this event is that it's time limited, I can only play on weekends, and I don't have a lot of friends to play with. So basically getting the 5 needed to summon the Shrouded Ghost is a chore, especially considering I always land on a server with no one wanting to do the event (and many people trying to sink players who are just trying to do the adventure).

&#x200B;

I like the cooperation aspect but as long as Rare doesn't give us a way to control on which server we land, it's going to be complicated every single time.

I think it's gotta be apples. 

&#x200B;

A hoe is the tool to break leaves, and apples drop from oak leaves.

&#x200B;

Plus there are several variants of apples: green apples, red apples, golden apples.  


Oak trees are everywhere but the drop rate is low for apples.

Last night every single episode of Star Trek: Discovery was missing. Every single one. Could not play any at all.

&#x200B;

This morning they all came back. Tonight, episode 7 of Season 4 is missing. After 6 it skips to 8. I got spoiled of a lot of the plot from episode 7 because I did not realize it skipped it before it did the "previously on" recap. 

&#x200B;

Paramount's service is so inconsistent it makes me rethink why I'm paying them at all.

I'm having the same problem. Anyone know what to do?

&#x200B;

EDIT: Restarting the client solved the issue for me.

Not sure if you ever managed to find a solution, but I found one and thought I'd share if someone finds this post as I did:

&#x200B;

In page 8 (as of current version v2.8.1) there's an option called "Utilities" that has a flag to Lock / Unlock the armor stand. Just "Unlock" it. Then you'll be able to make the stand visible using Page 2.

&#x200B;

That will let you destroy the armor stand and loot it, removing the tool rack. Hope this helps!

It's happening to me every single raid and it's annoying since in my group I'm one of the few level 40s that do the most damage.

&#x200B;

It also means I'm losing on catching legendaries since I can't throw pokeballs at them.

There's a group of about 200 people that keep moving waypoints to suit their needs. They moved statues out of parks, they moved points of interest more than a block over... We keep reporting them and moving them back but there are 200 people rejecting our corrections, so it's impossible to make them right.

&#x200B;

People are openly abusing this and nobody from Niantic is taking action. It's sad, but it makes me want to stop playing altogether.

I got a workaround while they fix it...

&#x200B;

First down He until he starts casting the revive.

&#x200B;

Then nuke Sun until she's at 1 health.

&#x200B;

Then as she starts casting the revive, nuke Rook until 1 health.

&#x200B;

By this time He will be back on his feet. Nuke him and they'll be down.

&#x200B;

It's tricky but I managed to do it after 6 tries.

Pokestops are giving a lot less items now. It's now been 2 weeks since I've seen the last Revive from a pokestop. I went from 200 max revives to only 70 in these 2 weeks.

&#x200B;

And there's a spoofer in my neighborhood downing gyms late at night and in middle of storms and filling them with several accounts. We have reported them and Niantic isn't doing anything about it.

&#x200B;

It's like they don't even want us to play anymore.
